1
00:00:02,252 --> 00:00:03,921
Oh, dear.

2
00:00:04,129 --> 00:00:06,882
Penny, have you been recording
shows on our DVR again?

3
00:00:07,090 --> 00:00:11,220
-No.
-Answer honestly. This is not a trial.

4
00:00:11,887 --> 00:00:13,597
That will come later.

5
00:00:13,805 --> 00:00:15,807
Absolutely not.

6
00:00:16,015 --> 00:00:19,019
Help me out here.
I can't afford another demerit.

7
00:00:19,853 --> 00:00:24,942
Uh, maybe we were hacked. The Chinese
have been hacking everything lately.

8
00:00:25,901 --> 00:00:30,029
Why would the Chinese make our DVR
record Paul Blart: Mall Cop?

9
00:00:32,031 --> 00:00:33,325
I don't know.

10
00:00:33,534 --> 00:00:36,286
It's a fat guy on a Segway.
That's funny everywhere.

11
00:00:37,371 --> 00:00:39,540
-I'm deleting it.
-Hang on.

12
00:00:39,748 --> 00:00:42,543
Maybe the Chinese
haven't finished watching it yet.

13
00:00:44,545 --> 00:00:46,588
If you're trying to make space on the DVR...

14
00:00:46,797 --> 00:00:50,801
...why don't you get rid of stuff
you've already watched? Like Alphas.

15
00:00:51,050 --> 00:00:53,595
No, that's the season-two finale.
Quite the cliffhanger.

16
00:00:53,804 --> 00:00:56,139
I'm gonna rewatch it
before season three starts.

17
00:00:56,348 --> 00:00:58,267
There's no season three.
They canceled that show.

18
00:01:01,979 --> 00:01:05,065
Well, they can't cancel it.
It ended on a cliffhanger.

19
00:01:06,149 --> 00:01:07,192
Well, they did.

20
00:01:07,401 --> 00:01:09,194
There are two dumplings left.
Want them?

21
00:01:09,403 --> 00:01:12,489
Dumplings? Don't you understand
what's going on here?

22
00:01:12,698 --> 00:01:14,575
As a rule, no.

23
00:01:15,576 --> 00:01:19,288
That show ended with all the residents
of New York either dead or unconscious.

24
00:01:19,496 --> 00:01:21,832
Now I'll never know what happened.

25
00:01:22,082 --> 00:01:23,875
Why don't you make up
your own ending?

26
00:01:24,083 --> 00:01:26,336
Oh. Sure, what a wonderful idea.

27
00:01:26,587 --> 00:01:29,548
And after that I'll make up my own rules
of oral hygiene...

28
00:01:29,756 --> 00:01:32,843
...and instead of flossing,
I'll rub pudding on my gums.

29
00:01:33,051 --> 00:01:35,721
I'm gonna get the number of
the Syfy Channel and give them what for.

30
00:01:35,929 --> 00:01:37,472
Oh, please don't do that.

31
00:01:37,681 --> 00:01:40,183
No. They can't just cancel
a show like Alphas.

32
00:01:40,392 --> 00:01:42,477
They have to help the viewers let go.

33
00:01:42,686 --> 00:01:45,188
Firefly did a movie to wrap things up.

34
00:01:45,397 --> 00:01:48,358
Buffy the Vampire Slayer
continued on as a comic book.

35
00:01:48,609 --> 00:01:51,695
Heroes gradually lowered the quality
season by season...

36
00:01:51,903 --> 00:01:53,739
...until we were grateful it ended.

37
00:01:54,948 --> 00:01:56,825
I feel bad for whoever gets that phone call.

38
00:01:57,034 --> 00:02:00,245
Ah, don't. If they didn't wanna be
yelled at by crazy nerds...

39
00:02:00,454 --> 00:02:02,664
...they shouldn't have started
a sci-fi channel.

40
00:02:27,606 --> 00:02:30,484
I think you're gonna be really happy
with this security camera.

41
00:02:30,692 --> 00:02:33,236
The optics are great.
It's got infrared technology.

42
00:02:33,445 --> 00:02:36,823
And there's even a backup battery
when the power goes out.

43
00:02:37,032 --> 00:02:39,660
Whatever. I can see my little princess
while I'm at work, right?

44
00:02:39,826 --> 00:02:41,078
The Closure Alternative

45
00:02:41,787 --> 00:02:44,623
Why can't you watch porn
like a regular guy?

46
00:02:46,625 --> 00:02:49,795
Give me your laptop so I can
configure the software.

47
00:02:50,003 --> 00:02:52,089
Hold on. This is weird.

48
00:02:52,297 --> 00:02:53,340
What?

49
00:02:53,548 --> 00:02:56,343
I was Googling that girl I've been dating
and found her blog.

50
00:02:56,551 --> 00:02:58,512
Cool. Anything juicy?

51
00:02:58,720 --> 00:03:01,890
She said she recently went
on a date with a guy named Roger.

52
00:03:03,725 --> 00:03:05,936
And he's Indian.

53
00:03:06,937 --> 00:03:09,064
And he's an astrophysicist too!

54
00:03:12,025 --> 00:03:14,111
-You know what's going on, don't you?
-Yes.

55
00:03:14,319 --> 00:03:18,156
Mommy was right.
American girls are sexually voracious devils.

56
00:03:19,324 --> 00:03:22,619
I can't believe I have to explain this.
People change names on blogs...

57
00:03:22,828 --> 00:03:26,623
...to protect their privacy. "Roger" is Raj.

58
00:03:26,832 --> 00:03:28,207
Oh.

59
00:03:28,417 --> 00:03:31,878
I always thought if I had a white name,
it would be Gavin.

60
00:03:34,005 --> 00:03:36,883
-Keep reading. What does it say?
-No, I don't know if I should.

61
00:03:37,092 --> 00:03:39,886
If she wanted me to know about her blog,
she would've told me.

62
00:03:40,095 --> 00:03:43,974
-It's almost like I'm reading her diary.
-It's exactly what it's like. Keep reading.

63
00:03:44,683 --> 00:03:46,143
No, this is creepy.

64
00:03:46,351 --> 00:03:50,856
Oh.... I think we were looking at creepy in the
rearview mirror when I put up that camera.

65
00:03:51,690 --> 00:03:55,485
It's not creepy. Don't listen to him.

66
00:03:55,694 --> 00:03:59,740
[IN BABY-TALK VOICE]
Ooh, who's got the sweetest kisses?

67
00:03:59,948 --> 00:04:01,950
[SMOOCHING]

68
00:04:08,373 --> 00:04:10,000
Should I go?

69
00:04:15,213 --> 00:04:18,550
With all the TV Sheldon was talking about,
I had the greatest idea ever.

70
00:04:18,759 --> 00:04:22,763
It blows away my idea for a Star Wars-themed
coffee shop called Brewbacca's.

71
00:04:25,348 --> 00:04:29,019
You need to watch Buffy the Vampire Slayer.
The perfect show for the two of us.

72
00:04:29,227 --> 00:04:33,315
It's got action and jokes and hot vampires
and romance. I cannot oversell this.

73
00:04:33,523 --> 00:04:34,858
What do you say?

74
00:04:35,567 --> 00:04:37,527
It's 6:30 in the morning.

75
00:04:40,030 --> 00:04:42,199
LEONARD:
I thought you grew up on a farm.

76
00:04:45,202 --> 00:04:50,123
Hello, Syfy Network,
this is your vice president of programming.

77
00:04:50,916 --> 00:04:54,294
We have made a horrible mistake
regarding Alphas.

78
00:04:54,503 --> 00:04:57,296
We need to uncancel it immediately.

79
00:04:57,506 --> 00:04:59,591
Put me through
to the people who handle that.

80
00:04:59,800 --> 00:05:02,719
Tell them it's me.
I don't wanna answer a lot of questions...

81
00:05:02,928 --> 00:05:04,763
...about if I really am who I say I am.

82
00:05:05,514 --> 00:05:07,516
I just-- I want this done.

83
00:05:08,350 --> 00:05:10,644
No, I'm not the person who just called.

84
00:05:12,521 --> 00:05:15,023
That man was clearly a cowboy...

85
00:05:15,941 --> 00:05:18,443
...concerned about y'all
canceling his favorite show.

86
00:05:20,946 --> 00:05:23,240
Why do they keep hanging up on me?

87
00:05:23,448 --> 00:05:24,866
I'm sorry you're upset.

88
00:05:25,075 --> 00:05:30,789
Sheldon, sometimes people seek the comfort
of physical contact in moments like this.

89
00:05:35,669 --> 00:05:39,798
I am not flying back to Texas
just so my mom can give me a hug.

90
00:05:42,133 --> 00:05:44,719
Okay. Well, what I think is going on here...

91
00:05:44,928 --> 00:05:47,639
...is you have a pathological need
for closure.

92
00:05:47,848 --> 00:05:49,891
Oh. That's nonsense.

93
00:05:50,100 --> 00:05:54,145
You tell me stories about your day
all the time. I don't care how they end.

94
00:05:56,481 --> 00:05:59,234
You know, I might be able
to help you with this.

95
00:05:59,442 --> 00:06:02,153
There's a field of behavioral neuroscience
that examines...

96
00:06:02,361 --> 00:06:05,866
...ways to retrain your neural pathways
so stuff like this bothers you less.

97
00:06:06,074 --> 00:06:08,827
But I just told you,
I don't have a problem with closure.

98
00:06:09,578 --> 00:06:11,663
-You sure about that?
-Quite sure.

99
00:06:23,925 --> 00:06:24,968
That proves nothing.

100
00:06:28,638 --> 00:06:31,516
-Ready to go to lunch?
-Do you think I'm feminine?

101
00:06:33,101 --> 00:06:36,479
-Yeah, let's go.
-Thanks a lot.

102
00:06:36,688 --> 00:06:40,650
-What's going on?
-I broke down and I read Lucy's blog.

103
00:06:40,859 --> 00:06:45,030
In one of the entries she said when we
first met, I struck her as a little feminine.

104
00:06:45,864 --> 00:06:48,325
Just a little? That's great.

105
00:06:49,159 --> 00:06:50,702
I have to talk to her about this.

106
00:06:50,911 --> 00:06:53,538
Ahh. Jeez, why do you girls always want
to talk about things?

107
00:06:54,873 --> 00:06:58,877
Listen to me, if she's writing about
your relationship, use it to your advantage.

108
00:06:59,127 --> 00:07:02,172
-Rig the game.
-That doesn't seem fair.

109
00:07:02,380 --> 00:07:06,843
Is it fair that girls like confident,
normal guys more than nervous weirdos?

110
00:07:07,052 --> 00:07:09,387
No, it's not.
I've always thought that was unfair.

111
00:07:10,639 --> 00:07:14,851
So take what's in that blog
and use it to get her pants off.

112
00:07:15,060 --> 00:07:18,813
Why do you make everything filthy?
Why couldn't you say the blog is like...

113
00:07:19,022 --> 00:07:20,982
...her giving me the key to her heart?

114
00:07:21,191 --> 00:07:24,361
"The key to her heart." Heh. That's nice.

115
00:07:24,569 --> 00:07:28,031
Were you quoting someone
or is it tattooed on the small of your back?

116
00:07:28,239 --> 00:07:33,954
I was quoting a man who knows a thing
or two about women: Sir Elton John.

117
00:07:38,833 --> 00:07:40,835
["BUFFY THE VAMPIRE PLAYER" THEME
PLAYING ON TV]

118
00:07:43,588 --> 00:07:48,301
So did you love it? Of course you
loved it. Tell me how much you loved it.

119
00:07:48,510 --> 00:07:49,594
It was cute.

120
00:07:52,305 --> 00:07:55,058
Aw, don't say "cute." That's the worst.

121
00:07:55,266 --> 00:07:58,144
-What's wrong with cute?
-It just makes things seem small.

122
00:07:58,353 --> 00:07:59,729
It diminishes them.

123
00:07:59,938 --> 00:08:03,191
So you want me to stop calling
your little tushy cute?

124
00:08:03,400 --> 00:08:06,361
You can try,
but nobody's gonna believe you.

125
00:08:08,780 --> 00:08:12,534
I don't understand how you can watch
a show that great and not be excited by it.

126
00:08:12,742 --> 00:08:16,329
-I liked it. I'm excited.
-Well, then tell your face.

127
00:08:17,747 --> 00:08:20,667
-What do you want from me?
-You know what? Never mind.

128
00:08:20,875 --> 00:08:22,836
We gave it a shot.
Let's just see what else is on.

129
00:08:23,044 --> 00:08:27,173
Oh, come on, don't be like that.
I'm sorry I called it cute.

130
00:08:27,382 --> 00:08:28,925
-Let's watch another one.
-Really?

131
00:08:29,134 --> 00:08:32,095
Yeah. It was fun.
It kind of reminded me of my high school.

132
00:08:32,303 --> 00:08:35,724
But instead of vampires,
we had meth-heads. Ahem.

133
00:08:36,808 --> 00:08:39,936
But both came out at night
and had messed up teeth.

134
00:08:40,145 --> 00:08:42,897
All right, cool.
I think you'll like the next one better.

135
00:08:43,106 --> 00:08:45,567
All the cheerleaders
are suffering from an evil curse.

136
00:08:45,775 --> 00:08:47,986
Oh. Well, that's like my high school too.

137
00:08:49,029 --> 00:08:51,281
But instead of a curse, it was crabs. Heh.

138
00:08:54,325 --> 00:08:58,455
I've come up with a series of exercises
to help with your compulsive need for closure.

139
00:08:58,663 --> 00:09:01,750
I take issue with the word "compulsive."

140
00:09:03,084 --> 00:09:08,506
All I'm saying is we live in a world
where closure isn't always an op--

141
00:09:19,684 --> 00:09:20,935
--tion! Okay!

142
00:09:23,271 --> 00:09:25,857
For the sake of argument,
let's say I have a problem.

143
00:09:26,066 --> 00:09:27,942
What would be your plan
for addressing it?

144
00:09:28,151 --> 00:09:30,487
I'm going to recondition your brain...

145
00:09:30,695 --> 00:09:35,033
...so that the need for completion
isn't so overwhelming.

146
00:09:37,202 --> 00:09:40,288
-By playing tic-tac-toe?
-Yep, your turn.

147
00:09:40,497 --> 00:09:44,209
Oh, Amy. And you wonder why
people think neuroscience...

148
00:09:44,417 --> 00:09:46,711
...is nothing but a goofy game
for diaper babies.

149
00:09:48,088 --> 00:09:51,841
Tic-tac-toe can only end
in win, lose or draw.

150
00:09:52,050 --> 00:09:56,721
None of which will deny me closure,
especially since I'm about to win.

151
00:10:07,816 --> 00:10:09,484
But we didn't finish.

152
00:10:10,193 --> 00:10:12,737
Exactly. How does that make you feel?

153
00:10:14,823 --> 00:10:16,783
The same way
any normal person would.

154
00:10:16,991 --> 00:10:20,870
Feel like I wanna peel off my own face,
tear it in two and then again and again...

155
00:10:21,079 --> 00:10:23,706
...until I have a handful of
Sheldon-face confetti.

156
00:10:24,749 --> 00:10:27,544
That's the feeling we want to address
with this treatment.

157
00:10:27,752 --> 00:10:31,589
Yeah. Or you could pitch in, grab a nostril
and help me get this face off.

158
00:10:31,840 --> 00:10:33,675
Come on. You can do this.

159
00:10:33,883 --> 00:10:36,678
You don't know what it's like
to feel completely frustrated.

160
00:10:36,886 --> 00:10:42,225
To have a desire build up within you
and be denied any opportunity for release.

161
00:10:49,899 --> 00:10:51,359
Yeah, sounds like a drag.

162
00:10:56,239 --> 00:10:58,241
["BUFFY THE VAMPIRE SLAYER" THEME
PLAYING ON TV]

163
00:11:02,120 --> 00:11:05,415
Okay, help me out here.
Why does he love this show so much?

164
00:11:05,623 --> 00:11:08,585
Well, there was action, it was funny.

165
00:11:08,793 --> 00:11:12,088
I mean, you do get that usually
the monster chases the pretty girl...

166
00:11:12,297 --> 00:11:14,757
...but this time the pretty girl
chases the monsters?

167
00:11:16,843 --> 00:11:20,013
Yippee, it's backwards, I get it.

168
00:11:21,222 --> 00:11:23,141
Why does this bother you so much?

169
00:11:23,349 --> 00:11:27,061
I don't know. It's just, he's so passionate
about so many different things.

170
00:11:27,270 --> 00:11:29,314
I just don't get that way. Do you?

171
00:11:29,522 --> 00:11:32,442
Well, sure.
I'm pretty passionate about science.

172
00:11:32,650 --> 00:11:37,155
I remember the first time I looked through
a microscope and saw tiny microorganisms.

173
00:11:37,363 --> 00:11:39,490
It was like a whole other universe.

174
00:11:39,698 --> 00:11:43,995
If I wanted to, I could wipe it out
with my thumb like a god.

175
00:11:45,955 --> 00:11:48,124
See, I wish I had
some of that fire in my life.

176
00:11:48,333 --> 00:11:51,628
I wanna care about things
and get excited like you guys.

177
00:11:51,836 --> 00:11:54,172
-There's no reason you can't.
-You think?

178
00:11:54,380 --> 00:11:58,843
Absolutely. All we need to do is spend time
and find something you're passionate about.

179
00:11:59,636 --> 00:12:02,347
Ugh, that sounds like a lot of work.

180
00:12:07,018 --> 00:12:08,269
Hey, what's up?

181
00:12:08,478 --> 00:12:10,480
Lucy's coming over. I need some advice.

182
00:12:10,688 --> 00:12:14,525
However long you think
the foreplay should be, triple it.

183
00:12:16,986 --> 00:12:19,447
Just tell me which one you think
is more manly.

184
00:12:19,656 --> 00:12:24,202
This hockey jersey or this football jersey?

185
00:12:24,953 --> 00:12:27,664
I don't know. Go with hockey.

186
00:12:27,872 --> 00:12:30,166
Good, black is more slimming.

187
00:12:31,376 --> 00:12:32,418
[KNOCKING ON DOOR]

188
00:12:32,627 --> 00:12:35,380
That's her. I gotta go be butch. Toodles.

189
00:12:40,510 --> 00:12:42,720
-[IN DEEP VOICE] Hey. Come in.
-Hi.

190
00:12:44,222 --> 00:12:48,351
-Aw. Look how cute your little doggie is.
-Yeah, I wouldn't get too close.

191
00:12:48,559 --> 00:12:51,479
If I give the right command in German,
she'll rip your face off.

192
00:12:56,401 --> 00:13:00,571
AMY [SINGING]:
O'er the land of the free

193
00:13:00,779 --> 00:13:05,827
And the home of the

194
00:13:06,035 --> 00:13:07,245
Next.

195
00:13:11,833 --> 00:13:13,584
That's an impressive layout, isn't it?

196
00:13:16,129 --> 00:13:17,839
Yes.

197
00:13:20,799 --> 00:13:22,093
Let's box it up.

198
00:13:24,929 --> 00:13:26,889
[IMITATES AMY]
Let's box it up.

199
00:13:29,767 --> 00:13:31,769
["POP GOES THE WEASEL"
PLAYING ON BOX]

200
00:13:35,565 --> 00:13:36,733
That's enough.

201
00:13:38,901 --> 00:13:41,154
-Sheldon, give it!
-No!

202
00:13:43,448 --> 00:13:46,159
Okay, Sheldon,
make a wish and blow out the candles.

203
00:13:52,874 --> 00:13:55,793
Oops. Missed one.
Now your wish can't come true.

204
00:13:58,796 --> 00:14:00,923
Lucky for you,
because I wished you were dead.

205
00:14:05,636 --> 00:14:08,598
-I like your jersey.
-Thanks, I love hockey.

206
00:14:08,806 --> 00:14:10,433
Cool, so does my dad.

207
00:14:10,641 --> 00:14:13,770
We watched it all the time growing up.
Who's your favorite player?

208
00:14:18,857 --> 00:14:22,278
Not Brian Boitano, that's for sure.

209
00:14:24,530 --> 00:14:27,825
-How's your burrito?
-Still a little frozen in the middle.

210
00:14:28,034 --> 00:14:32,121
Probably because I didn't read the instructions.
No wrapper's gonna tell me what to do.

211
00:14:32,330 --> 00:14:34,873
Unless his name is Jay-Z.

212
00:14:35,666 --> 00:14:38,294
-Is something going on?
-What do you mean?

213
00:14:38,503 --> 00:14:40,963
Well, you're acting all weird,
and I'm pretty weird...

214
00:14:41,172 --> 00:14:43,966
...so I think I know what I'm talking about.

215
00:14:44,175 --> 00:14:48,304
I don't know, maybe it's all those
steroids I've been taking.

216
00:14:49,680 --> 00:14:53,142
I think I'm gonna go. Thank you
for the burrito and the pork rinds...

217
00:14:53,351 --> 00:14:57,814
...and the 20-minute lecture on why
monster trucks are better than regular trucks.

218
00:14:58,022 --> 00:14:59,399
Wait, wait.

219
00:15:01,025 --> 00:15:04,195
I found your blog
where you wrote about me.

220
00:15:04,862 --> 00:15:09,117
Oh. I just write that for myself.
I didn't think anybody actually read it.

221
00:15:09,325 --> 00:15:13,079
No kidding. You didn't make it easy to find.
I spent hours digging around online.

222
00:15:14,705 --> 00:15:17,875
For the record, you have excellent credit
and your diabetic aunt...

223
00:15:18,084 --> 00:15:20,837
...seems to be adjusting to her new leg
just fine.

224
00:15:23,089 --> 00:15:25,049
Why were you acting so strange tonight?

225
00:15:26,384 --> 00:15:28,344
You called me "feminine."

226
00:15:28,553 --> 00:15:31,180
I wanted you to think I was more manly.

227
00:15:31,389 --> 00:15:34,058
Raj, I didn't say feminine was a bad thing.

228
00:15:34,267 --> 00:15:37,937
I meant you're sweet and thoughtful
and your skin looks so much like caramel...

229
00:15:38,146 --> 00:15:40,898
...I just want to dip an apple in your face.

230
00:15:41,983 --> 00:15:45,361
I do have a pretty balls-to-the-wall
moisturizing regimen.

231
00:15:46,362 --> 00:15:48,364
So are you okay?

232
00:15:49,240 --> 00:15:50,616
-Yeah.
-Good.

233
00:15:51,742 --> 00:15:54,829
-Do you even like hockey?
-Heh. No.

234
00:15:55,037 --> 00:15:58,458
I bought this at the Staples Center
when I went to see Taylor Swift.

235
00:16:01,294 --> 00:16:06,507
So I was thinking how excited you get
about stuff like Buffy or science...

236
00:16:06,716 --> 00:16:09,385
...or which TV remote
you and Sheldon should buy--

237
00:16:09,594 --> 00:16:12,138
The Harmony One was fine.
We didn't need the 1100...

238
00:16:12,388 --> 00:16:14,973
...which he knows is too big for my hand.

239
00:16:16,684 --> 00:16:19,270
See, that's the kind of passion
I didn't think I had.

240
00:16:19,479 --> 00:16:21,772
But then I realized
I'm passionate about you.

241
00:16:22,732 --> 00:16:26,444
Oh. My cute little tushy strikes again.

242
00:16:28,905 --> 00:16:32,408
I'm serious. I've always had these plans.
I was gonna be in movies...

243
00:16:32,617 --> 00:16:35,328
...and live this glamorous life,
and anything less than that...

244
00:16:35,536 --> 00:16:39,207
-...wasn't worth getting excited about.
-Those things can still happen.

245
00:16:39,415 --> 00:16:42,835
Obviously, it's gonna happen.
A psychic at a bachelorette party told me.

246
00:16:43,711 --> 00:16:47,965
Anyway, what I meant was
I shouldn't wait, you know?

247
00:16:48,174 --> 00:16:51,344
I've got you, I've got Sheldon...

248
00:16:51,552 --> 00:16:53,387
...and all these wonderful friends.

249
00:16:53,596 --> 00:16:55,598
My life is exciting right now.

250
00:16:57,141 --> 00:16:59,560
-That's a big deal.
-It is, isn't it?

251
00:16:59,769 --> 00:17:00,811
[CHUCKLES]

252
00:17:03,231 --> 00:17:06,317
So does that mean we get to do stuff
like talk about cool shows...

253
00:17:06,526 --> 00:17:10,655
...or get dressed up in matching costumes
and go to Comic-Con?

254
00:17:12,323 --> 00:17:14,825
Leonard, I had an epiphany, not a stroke.

255
00:17:18,829 --> 00:17:22,040
Amy, I must say, I was skeptical at first...

256
00:17:22,250 --> 00:17:25,086
...but this has truly been
a transformative evening.

257
00:17:25,294 --> 00:17:27,838
I'm a little surprised to hear you
feeling so positive.

258
00:17:28,047 --> 00:17:32,260
Well, you're an excellent neuroscientist,
you're a wonderful girlfriend...

259
00:17:32,468 --> 00:17:34,011
...and....

260
00:17:36,973 --> 00:17:40,893
-And?
-Doesn't matter, does it?

261
00:17:42,186 --> 00:17:43,980
I'm proud of you, Sheldon.

262
00:17:47,024 --> 00:17:49,193
And a complete sucker.

263
00:17:54,072 --> 00:17:55,366
Oh, yeah.

264
00:18:00,580 --> 00:18:02,582
["POP GOES THE WEASEL"
PLAYING ON BOX]

265
00:18:03,207 --> 00:18:05,918
There he is.

266
00:18:06,127 --> 00:18:08,004
["POP GOES THE WEASEL"
FINISHES PLAYING ON BOX]

267
00:18:08,629 --> 00:18:14,343
[SINGING]
And the home of the brave

268
00:18:17,888 --> 00:18:20,182
Don't stop. Yes, keep going.

269
00:18:20,391 --> 00:18:22,768
Just like that.
Almost there. Almost there.

270
00:18:22,977 --> 00:18:25,146
[MOANS]

271
00:18:28,774 --> 00:18:32,194
Sheldon, you big weirdo. I want you
to know I love that you're in my life.

272
00:18:32,403 --> 00:18:34,572
I love you too.

273
00:18:41,412 --> 00:18:46,876
Hello, is this the Bruce Miller
who wrote the season finale of Alphas?

274
00:18:47,710 --> 00:18:51,714
Oh, smashing. You already sound nicer
than the last Bruce Miller...

275
00:18:51,922 --> 00:18:56,552
...who suggested I have sexual relations
with myself. Now, down to business.

276
00:18:56,761 --> 00:18:58,596
Your show ended on a cliffhanger.

277
00:18:58,846 --> 00:19:01,891
Could you please tell me
how you planned to resolve it?

278
00:19:02,099 --> 00:19:03,726
Uh-huh.

279
00:19:03,934 --> 00:19:05,269
Mm-hm.

280
00:19:06,062 --> 00:19:07,897
I see.

281
00:19:08,105 --> 00:19:12,193
Well, that all stinks.
No wonder you got canceled. Bye.

282
00:19:13,069 --> 00:19:14,737
Ah.

